## Testing Strategy

**Smart test selection** -- never run the full suite unless explicitly asked.

1. Identify changed files: `git diff --name-only` + `git status --porcelain`
2. Map source files to test files (e.g., `UserService.swift` -> `UserServiceTests.swift`)
3. Include tests for any modified protocols or mocks
4. Run targeted: use multiple `-only-testing:{TEST_TARGET}/ClassName` flags

| Scope | When | Est. Time |
|-------|------|-----------|
| Single class | One file changed, isolated | ~5 sec |
| Related classes | Feature work, multiple files | ~30 sec |
| Full unit tests | Major refactoring, DI changes | ~5 min |
| All tests | Pre-release, CI, explicit request | varies |

## Git Workflow

When user expresses git intent, execute immediately:

| User Says | Action |
|-----------|--------|
| "commit" | `git add -A` + commit with conventional message |
| "push" | `git push origin {DEFAULT_BRANCH}` |
| "save" | Stage + commit + push |

Commit format: `type(scope): description` -- types: feat, fix, docs, test, refactor, chore

